  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania has received $22.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 443,323 awards with an average award size of $50.3K. Obligations are down 17.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $18.1B in obligations. AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP and FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC are the top two vendors with $5.5B and $4.2B respectively. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligation with $4.8B, followed by Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing with $3.7B. Aircraft Manufacturing accounts for $2B of obligations. FY2026 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date, so these figures reflect obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year. Use these totals to compare agency concentration, vendor concentration, and industry exposure within Pennsylvania federal contracting for FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 federal spending in Pennsylvania compare to prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations by fiscal year show $17.6B in FY21, $19.7B in FY22, $23.3B in FY23, $26.6B in FY24, $26.9B in FY25, and $22.3B in FY26. Obligations are down 17.2% year over year. Award activity in FY2026 to date totals 443,323 awards with an average award size of $50.3K. The FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 federal contracting in Pennsylvania?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $18.1B in obligations. The Department of Energy follows with $2B, and the Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $742M. AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP and FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC lead vendors with $5.5B and $4.2B respectively, and THE BOEING COMPANY and BECHTEL PLANT MACHINERY, INC. follow with $2.3B and $2.2B."
      }
    ]
  },
